  "description": "Stretches bright details into directional pixel-melt streaks while retaining the original RGB colours. Staggered strips sample a compressed region of the source image, then blend only bright sampled pixels back over the original. Adjust length, angle, strip width, brightness trigger, bleed, tail fade, source span (smaller spans produce longer stretches), lane variation and seed. Works especially well on neon lights, backlit portraits and high-contrast photography. Single-pass approximation: it does not sort pixels globally or reorder them by brightness.",
